 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "yevamot.87a.12",
   "daf": "87a",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "בַּת כֹּהֵן שֶׁנִּיסֵּת לְיִשְׂרָאֵל וְכוּ׳. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: ״וְשָׁבָה אֶל בֵּית אָבִיהָ״ — פְּרָט לְשׁוֹמֶרֶת יָבָם. ״כִּנְעוּרֶיהָ״ — פְּרָט לִמְעוּבֶּרֶת.",
   "en": "§ The Gemara returns to the mishna. The mishna taught: The «daughter of a priest married to an Israelite» may not partake of teruma. «The Sages taught: “And she is returned unto her father’s house”» (Leviticus 22:13); this «excludes a widow awaiting her yavam,» for she cannot go back to her father’s house as long as she is still waiting for the yavam to perform levirate marriage. «“As in her youth”;» this «excludes a pregnant woman,» as her pregnancy has changed her, and she is no longer as she was in her youth."
  }
 ],
